Pixel mode for level 1 compression

Add libdeflate_deflate_compress_sync_pixels(), for 32-bit pixels: at level 1
only whole pixels are matched - against the previous pixel, the pixel above,
and the most recent pixel with the same hash, using a small table that isn't
cleared for every call. On a TV streaming 4K video (1.4 GHz Cortex-A76) this
compresses video frames to about the same size as level 1, ~1.6x faster.

